---
import PolicyLayout from '~/layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/config/site';
import { ADS } from '~/config/ads';
const updated = 'September 25, 2026';
const analytics = Boolean((import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN ?? '').trim());
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Formatoza handles your data: files are converted in your browser and never uploaded. What limited data is processed for hosting, analytics and advertising."
  path="/privacy/"
  h1="Privacy policy"
  lead="The short version: the files you convert never leave your device. This policy explains the limited data that is processed when you visit the site."
  updated={updated}
>
  <h2>Your files</h2>
  <p>
    All converters on {SITE.name} process files locally in your web browser. The file you select or
    paste is read by code running on your device, converted there, and offered to you for download.{' '}
    <strong>
      Your files and their contents are never uploaded to our servers or to any third party
    </strong>
    , and we cannot see them. Converted files exist only in your browser tab's memory and disappear
    when you close the tab or start over.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some converters download additional code the first time you use them (for example a HEIC decoder
    or the PDF.js renderer). These are ordinary downloads of program code from our website; no
    information about your files is sent.
  </p>

  <h2>Information processed when you visit</h2>
  <h3>Hosting and security logs</h3>
  <p>
    The site is served by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical data needed
    to deliver pages and protect the site from abuse — such as your IP address, browser type, the
    page requested and the time of the request. See
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">
      Cloudflare's privacy policy
    </a>
    .
  </p>
  <h3>Analytics</h3>
  {analytics ? (
    <p>
      We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count page views. It does not use cookies or local storage,
      does not fingerprint visitors, and does not track you across sites.
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p>
      We currently do not use any analytics service. If we add one, it will be cookieless and this
      policy will be updated first.
    </p>
  )}
  <p>
    Our code is designed so that, if usage statistics are collected, only coarse information about a
    conversion can be recorded — which tool was used, whether it succeeded, and bucketed file
    counts, sizes and durations. File names, file contents, pasted text and error details are never
    included.
  </p>
  <h3>Advertising</h3>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is funded by advertising served by Google AdSense
    {ADS.enabled ? '' : ' (not active yet)'}. When advertising is active, Google and its partners
    use cookies and similar technologies to serve ads, limit how often you see an ad, measure
    performance and, where you have consented or where permitted, show personalised ads based on
    your visits to this and other websites.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on
      your visits to this and/or other sites on the Internet.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can opt out of personalised advertising in{' '}
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener">
        Google Ads Settings
      </a>{' '}
      or, for participating vendors, at{' '}
      <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">
        aboutads.info
      </a>
      .
    </li>
    <li>
      Learn more in{' '}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">
        How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services
      </a>
      .
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland are asked for consent
    through a consent management platform certified by Google before personalised ads or ad storage
    are used. Until you decide, advertising cookies are not used for personalisation. You can change
    your choice at any time via “Privacy choices” in the footer (shown when advertising is active).
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} itself does not set cookies. Advertising partners may set cookies as described
    above. See the <a href="/cookies/">cookie policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal bases (EEA, UK and Switzerland)</h2>
  <p>
    Hosting and security processing is based on our legitimate interest in operating a secure
    website. Advertising cookies and personalised advertising are based on your consent, which you
    can withdraw at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete or restrict the use
    of personal data, to object to processing, to data portability, and to complain to a
    data-protection authority. Residents of some US states may opt out of the “sale” or “sharing” of
    personal data for targeted advertising. Because we do not store files or accounts, we typically
    hold no personal data about you; requests relating to advertising data can also be made directly
    to Google. Contact us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is a general-audience tool and is not directed at children under 13. We do not
    knowingly collect personal data from children.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page when our practices change and revise the date above. Significant
    changes will be highlighted on this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
